<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were at the following levels, with week-ago and year-ago levels, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 5/9/96		  29/8/96		8/9/95</p>
<p>    Gasoline	425-450			400		   425</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75		    50-75		 50-75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,600		    1,600	 1,850-1,900</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    350			325		   425</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     20			 15		    25</p>
<p>Motor gasoline stocks were up as product arrived from ARA refineries and little left in barges to Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha inventories similarly rose as ARA refineries produced, but little product left.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks were steady as incoming cargoes from the former Soviet Union equalled outgoings to Benelux, Germany and Switzerland. Throughput of product was very quick.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories grew with some straight-run arrivals and some outgoing cracked to the bunker market and Germany.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks rose with the addition of blending material.</p>
<p>-- Philip Blenkinsop, Amsterdam Newsroom, 31 20 504 5000</p>
